Project Design Phase Phase

The Project Design Phase is the stage where the selected idea is planned and structured into a clear project. It explains how the project will be developed and how it will work.

Key steps:

1. Define objectives – Decide what the project should achieve.


2. Plan the features – Identify the main functions of the project.


3. Design the system – Create the structure, workflow, or layout.


4. Select tools and technologies – Choose suitable software, hardware, and programming languages.


5. Create a prototype – Prepare a basic model of the project.


6. Finalize the design – Review and improve the design before development.
